---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import { dynasties } from '../../data/dynasties';
---

<Layout title="Architecture Through the Dynasties | Chinese Architecture" description="Interactive timeline of Chinese architectural history from Shang to Qing. Compare styles and learn how each dynasty shaped China's built heritage.">
  <Nav />

  <section class="pt-24 pb-16 px-6 bg-stone-light">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <p class="text-vermillion text-sm font-medium tracking-widest uppercase mb-4 font-display">Timeline</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-4">Chinese Architecture Through the Dynasties</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted max-w-[65ch]">Each dynasty left its distinctive mark on China's architectural heritage. Explore 3,000 years of evolution in structure, style, and symbolism.</p>
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-[65ch] space-y-4 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
        <p>Architecture is the most durable record a dynasty leaves behind. When the Shang raised rammed-earth walls at Anyang, when the Han built timber towers over brick cores, when the Tang swept the world's largest capital city onto a grid of 108 wards — each period's buildings encoded its ambitions, its beliefs, and its available technology.</p>
        <p>This timeline presents nine major dynastic periods in order. Each entry summarizes the period's defining innovations and links to a full reference page covering structural systems, famous surviving monuments, and the cultural forces behind the style. For side-by-side comparison, open the <a href="/compare/" class="text-vermillion hover:text-vermillion-dark transition-colors">comparison tool</a>; for the building blocks that persist across all periods, see the <a href="/elements/" class="text-vermillion hover:text-vermillion-dark transition-colors">elements section</a>.</p>
        <p>If you are new to the subject, the Tang and Song dynasties make the best starting point — together they define the classical ideal of Chinese architecture, and their finest surviving structures (the Foguang Temple and the Yingxian Pagoda) can still be visited today.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 px-6 bg-stone-light">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto space-y-8">
      {dynasties.map((d, i) => (
        <a href={`/dynasties/${d.id}`} class="group block rounded-2xl border border-stone-dark/30 bg-stone hover:border-vermillion/20 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[280px_1fr]">
            <div class="aspect-[4/3] md:aspect-auto md:h-full overflow-hidden bg-stone-dark">
              <img src={d.image} alt={`${d.name} Dynasty architecture`} class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500" loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <div class="p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col justify-center">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-vermillion/10 text-vermillion text-xs font-medium">{d.years}</span>
              </div>
              <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-ink mb-2 group-hover:text-vermillion transition-colors">{d.name} Dynasty</h2>
              <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">{d.summary}</p>
              <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-sm text-ink mb-2">Key Features</h3>
              <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
                {d.features.slice(0, 3).map(f => (
                  <span class="text-xs text-ink-muted/70 bg-stone-light px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md">{f}</span>
                ))}
                {d.features.length > 3 && <span class="text-xs text-ink-muted/50 px-2.5 py-1">+{d.features.length - 3} more</span>}
              </div>
              <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-vermillion group-hover:gap-2.5 transition-all">
                Explore {d.name} architecture
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
